Hence,

$$\cos \angle AOC=\frac{\overrightarrow{CA}\cdot \overrightarrow{CO}}{|\overrightarrow{CA}| |\overrightarrow{CO}|}=\frac{-\frac{5}{2}\cdot \frac{5}{2}-\frac{9}{2}\cdot \frac{7}{2}+2\cdot \frac{5}{2}}{\sqrt{\frac{68}{4}+\frac{324}{4}+\frac{10}{4}}\sqrt{\frac{1}{4}+\frac{49}{4}+\frac{25}{4}}}=\frac{-\frac{25}{4}-\frac{63}{4}+5}{\sqrt{\frac{392}{4}}\sqrt{\frac{114}{4}}}=\frac{-\frac{83}{4}}{\sqrt{392}\sqrt{114}/2}=-\frac{83}{114\sqrt{2}}<0.$$  Thus, $\angle AOC$ is obtuse, which means that triangle $OAC$ is an acute-angled triangle with area less than half the area of triangle $OAB$.  Therefore, the area of triangle $OAB$ must be at least twice as large, so it follows that

