Let's consider a plane $\Pi_{i}$ with normal vector $\mathbf{n}_{i}$. The distance from a point $P(x,y,z)$ to $\Pi_{i}$ is given by
\[\frac{\left|\mathbf{n}_{i}\cdot(P)\right|}{\sqrt{\left|\mathbf{n}_{i}\right|^{2}}}=\frac{A_{i}}{B_{i}},\]
where $\mathbf{n}_{i}=(A_{i},B_{i},C_{i})$, $\mathbf{n}_{i}\cdot(P)=Ax+By+Cz=A_{i}x+B_{i}y+C_{i}z=Ax+By-Cz=-A_{i}x-B_{i}y+A_{i}z$, and $B_{i}x-A_{i}y=C_{i}z$.
We want $d_{i}=\frac{|A_i x+B_i y-C_i z|}{\sqrt{A_i^2+B_i^2+C_i^2}}$ so we have the system of equations
\begin{align*}
