& A_{2}x+B_{2}y-C_{2}z=A_{2}x+B_{2}y-C_{2}z \\
& A_{3}x+B_{3}y-C_{3}z=A_{3}x+B_{3}y-C_{3}z .
\end{align*}
The solution to this system is $(x,y)=(\frac{A_1C_2-A_2C_1}{A_1^2+B_1^2+C_1^2},\frac{B_1C_3-B_3C_1}{B_1^2+B_3^2+C_3^2})$.
In particular, if $d_1^2+d_2^2+d_3^2=36$ then the origin lies on all three planes, which means that the origin also satisfies the equation above for $A_i,B_i,C_i$ being $(1,0,-1),(1,-2,1),$ or $(1,1,1)$. This gives us three lines passing through the origin in $\mathbb{R}^3$ whose intersection forms an equilateral triangle centered at the origin (see below).

